From: icanc0 <ai7@vincentxie.net>
Date: 2026-08-21
Subject: [PATCH 3/N] board_loader: allow plot/export jobs to skip
 connectivity/DRC/class init

`BOARD_LOADER::initializeLoadedBoard()` unconditionally runs, for every load:

1. `DS_DATA_MODEL::LoadDrawingSheet` — the drawing sheet file.
2. Rebuild `ENUM_MAP<PCB_LAYER_ID>` — clear + repopulate.
3. Instantiate `DRC_ENGINE` and `InitEngine(rules)` — parses `.kicad_dru`.
4. Resolve DRC exclusions, add markers.
5. `BuildConnectivity()` — full ratsnest / connectivity graph build.
6. `BuildListOfNets()`.
7. `SynchronizeNetsAndNetClasses(true)`.
8. `SynchronizeComponentClasses()` — walk all footprints, apply project rules.
9. `SynchronizeTuningProfileProperties()`.

Steps 3-9 are needed only for interactive work, DRC, and BOM-style jobs.
For the plot / export commands (`svg`, `pdf`, `png`, `gerbers`, `drill`,
`dxf`, `ps`, `gencad`, `ipc2581`, `ipcd356`, `stackup`, `stats`) they are
pure overhead: the plotter walks board geometry directly and never asks the
connectivity graph or the DRC engine anything.

On the 5.6 MB `demos/video` board, these steps are the biggest chunk of the
~2.2 s post-`--version` overhead (see `benchmarks/00-baseline-*.md`).

Approach:

- Add fine-grained flags to `BOARD_LOADER::OPTIONS` (all default true → no
  behavior change for existing callers).
- `initializeLoadedBoard()` gates the corresponding steps.
- `PCBNEW_JOBS_HANDLER::getBoard()` picks minimal options when the job is a
  known-plot job (identified via `dynamic_cast<JOB_EXPORT_PCB_PLOT*>` on the
  base type, plus explicit whitelist for drill/gencad/etc. which don't
  descend from `_PLOT`).

Steps 1-2, the layer enum, and `SetProject` still run — the plotter reads
`GetLayerName()`, `GetPageSettings()`, and the design settings.

